## Context & Background

### What This Is About

This project implements C/AS2 fire safety systems with 13 note evaluators that modify base systems based on building conditions. Notes can:
- **Remove systems** (e.g., Note 1a removes Type 2 for small SM buildings)
- **Add systems** (e.g., Note 7 adds Type 3 for WB warehouses)
- **Track compliance** (e.g., Note 3 tracks dual water supply requirements)
- **Apply cross-firecell** (e.g., Note 9 applies to ALL VP if ANY triggers)

**Current Coverage:**
- ✅ Note 4: Early childhood centres - 6 tests (COMPLETE)
- ❌ Notes 1a, 1b, 1c, 1d: No integration tests
- ❌ Notes 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8: No integration tests
- ❌ Notes 9, 10: No integration tests
- ❌ Complex multi-firecell scenarios: No tests

### Why Integration Tests Matter

Unit tests verify individual note evaluators work in isolation. Integration tests verify:
- Orchestrator calls note evaluators correctly
- Cross-firecell dependencies work (notes 1b, 1c, 9, 10)
- System modifications persist through the pipeline
- Compliance info is stored correctly
- Multiple notes can coexist without conflicts

These are the tests that catch real-world bugs.

